{
  "contract": "C4 (set_scopes), C10 (the allowlist line) and C11 (the relay's keys), docs/protocol.md, since board ab-v16.30. The receiver (part 1a, board ab-v16.31) applies set_scopes, and the relay (part 2, boards ab-v16.35 and ab-v16.36) applies the allowlist line, by the same rules; both check their code against these vectors. Every value is a sample.",
  "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$",
  "casesNote": "in: the fields of a set_scopes request (or of an allowlist line). applies: what applies (lists, scopes, default and operator after the rules; a scope or list that applies as absent is not there). refused: the count in the answer. listOf: the list that a scope gets (null: no list), also for a scope that scopes does not name.",
  "cases": [
    {"note": "The design's example (section 8.1): two lists, three scopes, no default.", "in": {"lists": {"marketdata": ["marketdata.app", "github.com"], "vedlo": ["vedlo.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "marketdata", "md-worker-2": "marketdata", "vedlo-cron": "vedlo"}, "default": null}, "applies": {"lists": {"marketdata": ["marketdata.app", "github.com"], "vedlo": ["vedlo.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "marketdata", "md-worker-2": "marketdata", "vedlo-cron": "vedlo"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {"md-lead": "marketdata", "vedlo-cron": "vedlo", "md-new": null}},
    {"note": "A scope with null, or whose list is a valid name that is not in lists, has no list and never falls back to default; a scope that scopes does not name gets default. None of them counts. A value that is a string but not a valid name counts 1 and applies as null (the same count as for default and operator).", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "md-none": null, "md-gone": "nolist", "md-bad-name": "not a name"}, "default": "md"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "md-none": null, "md-gone": "nolist", "md-bad-name": null}, "default": "md", "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md", "md-none": null, "md-gone": null, "md-bad-name": null, "md-new": "md"}},
    {"note": "A default that is not in lists gives no list, with no count.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": "nolist"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": "nolist", "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {"md-new": null}},
    {"note": "Entries that are not normalized are refused, 1 each; the other entries of the list apply.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example", "A.example", "https://a.example/", "*.a.example", "a.example.", "localhost", "10.0.0.1", 5, null, "sub.a.example", "xn--bcher-kva.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example", "sub.a.example", "xn--bcher-kva.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 8, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md"}},
    {"note": "A list whose name does not match the pattern, or whose value is not an array, applies as absent: 1, and 1 more for each entry of its array. A scope of such a list has no list.", "in": {"lists": {"bad name": ["a.example", "b.example"], "-x": [], "": ["a.example"], ".y": "a.example", "md": "a.example", "ok": ["c.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "md-ok": "ok"}, "default": null}, "applies": {"lists": {"ok": ["c.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "md-ok": "ok"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 8, "listOf": {"md-lead": null, "md-ok": "ok"}},
    {"note": "A scope that does not match the pattern applies as absent and counts 1. A scope that matches it but whose value is neither a string nor null applies as null and counts 1: it has no list and never falls back to default.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"], "other": ["b.example"]}, "scopes": {"a/b": "md", "": "md", "md-lead": 5, "md-x": ["md"], "md-y": {"list": "md"}, "md-ok": "md"}, "default": "other"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"], "other": ["b.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": null, "md-x": null, "md-y": null, "md-ok": "md"}, "default": "other", "operator": null}, "refused": 5, "listOf": {"md-ok": "md", "md-lead": null, "md-x": null, "md-y": null, "md-new": "other"}},
    {"note": "A scopes that is not an object makes default apply as null: no scope gets the default list.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": ["md-lead"], "default": "md"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {"md-lead": null, "md-new": null}},
    {"note": "A default that is neither a valid name nor null counts 1 and applies as null.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": ["md"]}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md", "md-new": null}},
    {"note": "A default that is a string but not a valid name counts 1 and applies as null, as the operator field does.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": "not a name"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md", "md-new": null}},
    {"note": "A missing default counts as one that is not a string or null.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md", "md-new": null}},
    {"note": "A lists or scopes that is not an object applies as an empty object and counts 1.", "in": {"lists": [["md", ["a.example"]]], "scopes": "md-lead", "default": null}, "applies": {"lists": {}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 2, "listOf": {"md-lead": null}},
    {"note": "A missing lists, scopes and default: 1 each.", "in": {}, "applies": {"lists": {}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 3, "listOf": {"md-lead": null}},
    {"note": "An empty list applies: its scope is admitted and can open about:blank only; it has no scope rule (C5).", "in": {"lists": {"empty": []}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "empty"}, "default": null}, "applies": {"lists": {"empty": []}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "empty"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {"md-lead": "empty"}},
    {"note": "The operator field (choice 3): \"*\".", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "*"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "*"}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The operator field: a list name in lists.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"], "operator-union": ["a.example", "b.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "operator-union"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"], "operator-union": ["a.example", "b.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "operator-union"}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The operator field: a valid name that is not in lists applies as null, with no count.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "gone"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The operator field: null, as when it is absent.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The operator field: any other value counts 1 and applies as null (a string that does not match the pattern).", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": "all sites"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The operator field: a number counts 1 and applies as null.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": 1}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 1, "listOf": {}},
    {"note": "The counts add up: a bad entry (1), a list that is not an array (1), a bad scope (1), a bad operator (1).", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example", "A.example"], "x": {}}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "-bad": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": ["*"]}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 4, "listOf": {"md-lead": "md"}},
    {"note": "Names that are also properties of a JavaScript object (constructor, toString, hasOwnProperty, valueOf) are names like any other; __proto__ does not match the pattern. A scope that scopes does not name gets default, also valueOf.", "in": {"lists": {"constructor": ["a.example"], "__proto__": ["b.example"], "toString": ["c.example"]}, "scopes": {"toString": "constructor", "hasOwnProperty": null, "__proto__": "constructor", "md-lead": "toString"}, "default": "constructor"}, "applies": {"lists": {"constructor": ["a.example"], "toString": ["c.example"]}, "scopes": {"toString": "constructor", "hasOwnProperty": null, "md-lead": "toString"}, "default": "constructor", "operator": null}, "refused": 3, "listOf": {"toString": "constructor", "hasOwnProperty": null, "md-lead": "toString", "valueOf": "constructor", "__proto__": "constructor"}},
    {"note": "A list name that is a property of a JavaScript object, and no such list: a scope or default that names it has no list.", "in": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "constructor", "md-x": "hasOwnProperty"}, "default": "toString", "operator": "valueOf"}, "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "constructor", "md-x": "hasOwnProperty"}, "default": "toString", "operator": null}, "refused": 0, "listOf": {"md-lead": null, "md-x": null, "constructor": null, "md-new": null}}
  ],
  "rawNote": "A request as the bytes that the receiver parses.",
  "raw": [
    {"note": "A name that comes twice in one object: the last one applies (JSON.parse and Python's json read it so). The daemon never sends one.", "json": "{\"lists\":{\"md\":[\"a.example\"],\"md\":[\"b.example\"]},\"scopes\":{\"md-lead\":\"md\",\"md-lead\":null},\"default\":null}", "applies": {"lists": {"md": ["b.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": null}, "default": null, "operator": null}, "refused": 0}
  ],
  "linesNote": "The relay's allowlist line (C10, C11). keysOn: the relay runs with --keys. keys: the keys map that applies (null: keys are off), or failClosed: true (the line applies no list).",
  "lines": [
    {"note": "With keys on: the keys map applies.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}}, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}},
    {"note": "With keys on: a line with no keys field gives no entry (every named scope gets the key's 403).", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null}, "keys": {}},
    {"note": "With keys on: keys that is not an object applies as an empty object.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": [["md-lead", "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"]]}, "keys": {}},
    {"note": "With keys on: keys null applies as an empty object.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": null}, "keys": {}},
    {"note": "With keys on: an entry whose value is not 64 lowercase hex digits applies as absent.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md", "md-a": "md", "md-b": "md", "md-c": "md", "md-d": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e", "md-a": "A8AE6E6EE929ABEA3AFCFC5258C8CCD6F85273E0D4626D26C7279F3250F77C8E", "md-b": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8", "md-c": 5, "md-d": ""}}, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}},
    {"note": "With keys on: an entry for a scope that does not match the pattern applies as absent.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e", "a/b": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}}, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}},
    {"note": "With keys on: scopes named like JavaScript object properties; toString has no entry.", "keysOn": true, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"constructor": "md", "toString": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": {"constructor": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e", "__proto__": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}}, "keys": {"constructor": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}},
    {"note": "Without keys: a line with a keys field (any value) applies no list, as if no line had come (the fourth not-ready 503; open connections close).", "keysOn": false, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": {"md-lead": "a8ae6e6ee929abea3afcfc5258c8ccd6f85273e0d4626d26c7279f3250f77c8e"}}, "failClosed": true},
    {"note": "Without keys: also keys null.", "keysOn": false, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "keys": null}, "failClosed": true},
    {"note": "Without keys: a line without keys applies as set_scopes does.", "keysOn": false, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null}, "keys": null},
    {"note": "The relay ignores the operator field: a bad value changes nothing that it applies.", "keysOn": false, "line": {"t": "allowlist", "lists": {"md": ["a.example"]}, "scopes": {"md-lead": "md"}, "default": null, "operator": "all sites"}, "keys": null}
  ]
}
